From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 11:55:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Treat file names, attributes and supersede as Windows
 11 does.

Measured on Windows 11 build 29671 with tools/finalpathprobe
(trailingprobe.c, finalpathprobe.c) and tools/fileattrprobe
(archiveprobe.c):

- A file's name with a backslash after it is no directory's: opening,
  creating, querying, copying, moving or deleting by it is
  STATUS_NOT_A_DIRECTORY (ERROR_DIRECTORY), unless a directory was to
  be created by it, which is STATUS_OBJECT_NAME_COLLISION; nothing but
  a directory is created by a new name with one.  Wine said
  STATUS_OBJECT_NAME_INVALID, as Windows before 11 did.
- A file superseded is emptied even when no write access is asked
  for, and even when it is read-only (wineserver).
- The name a file is opened by comes back, from FileNameInformation,
  NtQueryObject and GetFinalPathNameByHandle(FILE_NAME_OPENED), in the
  case it has on disk; a short name in capitals, the drive letter too.
  The loader's names keep the case they were asked for.
- The archive attribute is kept: a new or written-over file has it, a
  directory only when asked for; once cleared it comes back when the
  file is written to, made larger or smaller, renamed or linked.  The
  temporary, offline and not-indexed attributes are kept too; a file
  with none says FILE_ATTRIBUTE_NORMAL.  The extended attribute that
  keeps them is changed before a file is made read-only, and a
  read-only file is made writable for the while: making a hidden file
  read-only left it hidden.
- Setting a valid data length needs SeManageVolumePrivilege enabled.
- GetVolumePathName keeps the drive letter in the case it was given.
- scrrun's MoveFolder takes ERROR_DIRECTORY as a path not found.

Tests: new ones for the trailing backslash, supersede, the name case
and the archive attribute; expectations moved to Windows 11's results
(older ones kept as broken); todo_wine removed where Wine now passes,
also for SeCreateSymbolicLinkPrivilege, which advapi32 knows.  On
Windows the ntdll file and path, kernel32 file and volume, and scrrun
filesystem tests have no failures.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

